&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;During the third quarter of 2025, the Company completed a sale of land at the Yadkin site. Upon closing of the transaction, the Company received $2,758,999 and recorded a net gain of $2,729,100 in Miscellaneous non-operating (income) expenses, net, which can be found in Proceeds from Disposal of Noncurrent Assets on the cash flow statement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;On February 1, 2017, Alcoa completed the sale of the Yadkin Hydroelectric Project to Cube Hydro Carolinas (Cube). As part of the sales agreement, Alcoa retained the right to receive contingent consideration from Cube based on post-closing sales of Renewable Energy Credits (RECs) generated by the Yadkin Hydroelectric Project. For a period of up to 10 years after closing (through January 31, 2027), if RECs are sold for more than $5 per REC, the amount of the sales price &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;in excess of&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; $5 (multiplied by the number of RECs sold) is shared equally between Alcoa and Cube Hydro, subject to an aggregate cap of $20,000,000.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Beginning in 2024, Cube began paying Alcoa its share of RECs sold. During 2025 and 2024, Alcoa recorded a gain within miscellaneous non-operating income of $1,385,381 and $5,447,244, respectively, to reflect payments to Alcoa for the Company&amp;#8217;s portion of RECs sold by Cube.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Alcoa Power Generation, Inc. (APGI) and Southern Indiana gas and Electric Company (SIGECO) own 50% of Warrick Unit 4 and all associated components to generate electricity. APGI and SIGECO entered into a Joint Operating Agreement (JOA) in April 1958 as amended in September 2017 for the operation and maintenance of Unit 4. In accordance with the terms of the JOA, the agreement expired on December 31, 2023.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;On January 1, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;2024&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; APGI and SIGECO entered into an interim agreement for APGI&amp;#8217;s operation of 100% of Unit 4, with the following terms:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul style="margin: 0pt; padding-left: 0pt;" type="disc"&gt;
&lt;li style="margin-top: 14pt; margin-left: 27.6pt; padding-left: 8.4pt; font-family: serif; font-size: 10pt; -aw-font-family: 'Symbol'; -aw-font-weight: normal; -aw-number-format: '&amp;#61623;';"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;SIGECO will transfer its 50% ownership interest to APGI for consideration of $3 million (purchase transaction), pending regulatory approvals.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style="margin-left: 27.6pt; padding-left: 8.4pt; font-family: serif; font-size: 10pt; -aw-font-family: 'Symbol'; -aw-font-weight: normal; -aw-number-format: '&amp;#61623;';"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;Extends the JOA and gives operational control to APGI with 100% of revenue and expenses until the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;earlier&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 11pt;"&gt; of May 31, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 11pt;"&gt; or the closing of the purchase transaction.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 11pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style="margin-left: 27.6pt; padding-left: 8.4pt; font-family: serif; font-size: 10pt; -aw-font-family: 'Symbol'; -aw-font-weight: normal; -aw-number-format: '&amp;#61623;';"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;APGI provides SIGECO 150 MW Capacity from June 2024 through May 2025 at no cost.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style="margin-left: 27.6pt; margin-bottom: 14pt; padding-left: 8.4pt; font-family: serif; font-size: 10pt; -aw-font-family: 'Symbol'; -aw-font-weight: normal; -aw-number-format: '&amp;#61623;';"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;In May 2025, APGI paid SIGECO $3,000,000 for the remaining 50% ownership of Warrick Unit 4, which can be found in Gross Additions to Utility Plant on the cash flow statement. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol style="margin: 0pt; padding-left: 0pt;" start="5" type="A"&gt;
&lt;li style="margin-left: 15.09pt; padding-left: 2.91pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Leases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; color: #212529;"&gt;Management records a right-of-use asset and lease liability on the Company&amp;#8217;s balance sheet for building and equipment leases. These amounts are equivalent to the aggregate future lease payments on a discounted basis. The leases have remaining terms of less than 1 year to 6 years. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; color: #212529;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; color: #212529;"&gt;Lease expense and operating cash flows for the year ended December 31, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; color: #212529;"&gt;2024&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; color: #212529;"&gt; includes costs from third party operating leases of $425,256 and short-term rental expense of $196,898. There were no related party operating leases.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; color: #212529;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; color: #212529;"&gt;Lease expense and operating cash flows for the year ended December 31, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; color: #212529;"&gt;2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; color: #212529;"&gt; includes costs from third party operating leases of $544,852 and short-term rental expense of $277,762. There were no related party operating leases.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; color: #212529;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; color: #212529;"&gt;RoU assets obtained in exchange for new capitalized operating lease liability: $642,090.95. There were five new leases added during 2025. The Company does not have financing leases.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; color: #212529;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
