&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Future cash flows related to short term leases are $97,336 in 2025.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol style="margin: 0pt; padding-left: 0pt;" start="6" type="A"&gt;
&lt;li style="margin-left: 14.47pt; padding-left: 3.53pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Investments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Equity investments are primarily comprised of investments in APM LLC, an entity that purchases and sells power for use by Alcoa and its subsidiaries and affiliates and AAMI, an entity that owns and sells emissions credits for sulfur dioxide and nitrogen oxide.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;As non-regulated subsidiaries, APM LLC and AAMI are recorded as equity investments of APGI for FERC reporting purposes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;There were no equity investment balances as of December 31, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; and 2024. In accordance with the guidance in ASC 323, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-style: italic;"&gt;Investments &amp;#8211; Equity Method and Joint Ventures&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;, the Company discontinued applying the equity method and recording equity losses when the investment balance was reduced to zero. The Company will resume applying the equity method after its share of net income equals the share of net losses not recognized during the periods the application of equity method accounting was discontinued.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol style="margin: 0pt; padding-left: 0pt;" start="7" type="A"&gt;
&lt;li style="margin-left: 16.31pt; padding-left: 1.69pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Income Taxes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The (benefit)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; provision for taxes on income consisted of the following for the years ended December 31:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
