&lt;td style="width: 79.2pt; border-bottom-style: solid; border-bottom-width: 0.75pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: top;"&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: right; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;6,401,416&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 7.2pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: top;"&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: right; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 71.5pt; border-bottom-style: solid; border-bottom-width: 0.75pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: top;"&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: right; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;350,036 &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 80.8pt; border-bottom-style: solid; border-bottom-width: 0.75pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: top;"&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: right; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;5,570,187&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Deferred income taxes result primarily from differences between financial and income tax reporting for depreciation and employee benefit costs. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol style="margin: 0pt; padding-left: 0pt;" start="8" type="A"&gt;
&lt;li style="margin-left: 16.31pt; padding-left: 1.69pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Retirement Plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Company participates in Alcoa retirement plans and provides coverage under the plans &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;to&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; most employees.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Pension benefits generally depend upon length of service, job grade, and remuneration.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; Substantially all benefits are paid through pension trusts that are sufficiently funded to ensure that all plans can pay benefits to retirees as they become due.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Most salaried and non-union hourly employees hired after March 1, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;2006&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; participate in a defined contribution plan instead of a defined benefit plan.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The costs of participation in the plans are borne by the Company and are billed by Alcoa to APGI.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The billing is determined using the unit credit actuarial method, with unfunded prior service costs amortized over the average remaining service period of employees expected to receive benefits under the plans.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; Retirement plan costs included in operating (benefits) expenses were $76,827 in 2025 and ($19,004) in 2024.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Company maintains health care and life insurance benefit plans covering eligible retired employees under benefit plans sponsored by Alcoa.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Generally, the medical plans pay a percentage of medical expenses, reduced by deductibles and other coverages. These plans are generally unfunded, except for certain benefits funded through &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;a trust&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Life benefits are generally provided by insurance contracts.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; Alcoa retains the right, subject to existing agreements, to change or eliminate these benefits.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;All salaried and certain hourly employees hired after January 1, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;2002&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; will not have postretirement health care benefits. All salaried and certain hourly employees that retire on or after April&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;1, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;2008&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; are not eligible for post-retirement life insurance benefits. Total costs of post-retirement health care and life insurance benefits were ($1,995) in 2025 and ($3,253) in 2024. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Company also participates in defined contribution savings plans sponsored by Alcoa. The Company's employees may contribute a portion of their compensation to these plans, and Alcoa matches, mostly in company stock, a portion of these contributions. These expenses were $897,602 in 2025 and $788,027 in 2024. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol style="margin: 0pt; padding-left: 0pt;" start="9" type="A"&gt;
&lt;li style="margin-left: 12.03pt; padding-left: 5.97pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Derivatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Fair value is defined as the price that would be received to sell an asset or paid to transfer a liability in an orderly transaction between market participants at the measurement date. The fair value hierarchy distinguishes between (1) market participant assumptions developed based on market data obtained from independent sources (observable inputs) and (2) an entity&amp;#8217;s own assumptions about market participant assumptions developed based on the best information available in the circumstances (unobservable inputs). The fair value hierarchy consists of three broad levels, which gives the highest priority to unadjusted quoted prices in active markets for identical assets or liabilities (Level 1) and the lowest priority to unobservable inputs (Level 3). The three levels of the fair value hierarchy are described below:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#8226;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Level 1 - Unadjusted quoted prices in active markets that are accessible at the measurement date for identical, unrestricted assets or liabilities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#8226;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Level 2 - Inputs other than quoted prices included within Level 1 that are observable for the asset or liability, either directly or indirectly, including quoted prices for similar assets or liabilities in active markets; quoted prices for identical or similar assets or liabilities in markets that are not active; inputs other than quoted prices that are observable for the asset or liability (e.g., interest rates); and inputs that are derived principally from or corroborated by observable market data by correlation or other means.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#8226;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Level 3 - Inputs that are both significant to the fair value measurement and unobservable.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;During 2008, the Company entered into a power supply agreement with Public Utility District No. 1 of Chelan County, Washington (Chelan PUD) that contains a pricing provision related to a credit rating premium (CRP). The CRP is a monthly payment based on a credit rating spread between Chelan PUD and Alcoa credit ratings and is considered an embedded credit derivative. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The power supply agreement indexes the difference between the long-term debt ratings of Alcoa and Chelan PUD, the counterparty, from any of the three major credit rating agencies. If the counterparty&amp;#8217;s lowest credit rating is greater than one rating category above Alcoa&amp;#8217;s credit ratings, an independent investment banker would be consulted to determine a hypothetical interest rate for both parties. The two interest rates would be &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;netted&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; and the resulting difference would be multiplied by Alcoa&amp;#8217;s equivalent percentage of the outstanding principal of the counterparty&amp;#8217;s debt obligation as of December 31 of the year preceding the calculation date. This differential would be added to the cost of power in the period following the calculation date. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;There is an embedded credit derivative liability as of December 31, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; of $321,005. There was an embedded credit derivative liability as of December 31, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;2024&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; of $1,738,307. The fair value of the embedded derivative is included in Level 3. There were no transfers in or out of Levels 1, 2, or 3 of the fair value hierarchy during the periods presented.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The embedded credit derivative does not qualify for hedge accounting treatment. As &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;such, (&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;gains) and losses related to the change in fair value of the embedded derivative are recorded directly in other income deductions, net on the accompanying Statement of Income.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;2024:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 10.34pt; display: inline-block;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 36pt; display: inline-block;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 36pt; display: inline-block;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 36pt; display: inline-block;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 36pt; display: inline-block;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 36pt; display: inline-block;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 36pt; display: inline-block;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Embedded Credit Derivative ($):&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;January 1, 2024&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 2.04pt; display: inline-block;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 36pt; display: inline-block;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 36pt; display: inline-block;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 36pt; display: inline-block;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 36pt; display: inline-block;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 36pt; display: inline-block;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 36pt; display: inline-block;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 36pt; display: inline-block;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-style: italic;"&gt;Total Gains/Losses Included In:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Other Expenses, Net (Unrealized/Realized):&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 22.36pt; display: inline-block;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 36pt; display: inline-block;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 27.75pt; display: inline-block;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;2,493,958&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Settlements and Other:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 7.19pt; display: inline-block;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 36pt; display: inline-block;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 36pt; display: inline-block;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 36pt; display: inline-block;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 36pt; display: inline-block;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 27.75pt; display: inline-block;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;755,651)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;December 31, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;2024&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 21.56pt; display: inline-block;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 36pt; display: inline-block;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 36pt; display: inline-block;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 36pt; display: inline-block;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 36pt; display: inline-block;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 22.25pt; display: inline-block;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;1,738,307&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-style: italic;"&gt;Change In Unrealized Gains/Losses Included &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-style: italic;"&gt;In&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-style: italic;"&gt; Earnings&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 19.79pt; display: inline-block;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-style: italic;"&gt;(For Derivative Instruments Held &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-style: italic;"&gt;At&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-style: italic;"&gt; December 31, 2024):&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
